WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.680
Netflix has been putting out original&nbsp;
programming for almost six years — so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:07.120
it'll come as no surprise to find they've&nbsp;
gotten pretty good at it. From thrilling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:12.160
adventure flicks to sci-fi spectacles, these&nbsp;
are the best Netflix originals in 2021 so far.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:16.000
The rise of the gig economy has changed&nbsp;
the way people get ahead in the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.560
and The White Tiger plays with this idea in a&nbsp;
masterful way. The film focuses on a young man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:25.200
named Balram, who grows up in India and decides&nbsp;
at a young age that he's destined for greatness.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.960
However, India's rigid class system&nbsp;
has other things in store for him.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:33.040
Balram tries to get ahead as best he can with&nbsp;
the situation he's put in, working as a driver&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:37.840
for a wealthy family. However, opportunities are&nbsp;
few and far between, and Balram has to do some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:42.240
pretty awful things in order to achieve what&nbsp;
he believes is his destiny. Lead actor Adarsh&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:46.560
Gourav is so charismatic, and The White Tiger is&nbsp;
shot so beautifully that it's easy to get caught&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:50.800
up in the film's world — making the horrific&nbsp;
nature of its third act even more shocking.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:54.320
The White Tiger has been noted for its&nbsp;
similarities to the Oscar-winning classic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:58.960
Parasite, and like that movie, it defies any&nbsp;
kind of genre-tagging. With a killer cast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:03.120
great script, and near-faultless direction,&nbsp;
this is a compelling under-the-radar watch.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:08.960
It's easy to dismiss Finding 'Ohana as a retread&nbsp;
of a movie you've seen a dozen times before. A&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:13.040
ragtag group of kids band together to discover&nbsp;
a set of clues, find some hidden treasure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:17.040
and of course, learn more about themselves&nbsp;
along the way. It's The Goonies; it's Holes;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:21.680
it's Stranger Things. But Finding 'Ohana stands&nbsp;
out from these stories in some very distinct ways.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:26.240
For one, the movie is well aware that the audience&nbsp;
knows this song already. Finding 'Ohana has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:30.720
praised by some critics for wasting no time on&nbsp;
its first act and instead setting up higher stakes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:35.120
once the protagonists start hunting for treasure.&nbsp;
Even more impressive is the beautiful backdrop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:39.600
of Hawaiian scenery and culture. Finding 'Ohana&nbsp;
does a great job of showcasing its breathtaking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:44.080
vistas and unique cultural components to&nbsp;
make the whole film feel new and exciting.

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:48.000
Finding 'Ohana is a family-friendly adventure&nbsp;
with just enough nostalgia and beauty to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:53.840
keep adults invested, alongside a heap of&nbsp;
adventure and goofiness to win over the kids.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.160
"That smells like the butthole to hell."

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:02.560
Unless you happen to live in the British&nbsp;
countryside, it's likely that you could do with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:07.040
little more scenery like this in your life. Throw&nbsp;
in a fascinating period piece and a few fantastic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:12.880
actors, and you have what's probably Netflix's&nbsp;
highest-profile film of 2021 so far: The Dig.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:18.000
Based on the 2007 novel by John Preston, The&nbsp;
Dig stars Ralph Fiennes and Carey Mulligan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:21.360
Set in the late 1930s, Mulligan&nbsp;
plays a woman named Edith Pretty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:26.400
who hires archeologist Basil Brown to excavate the&nbsp;
land around her property. As Brown gets further&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:30.960
along in his dig, however, he realizes that he&nbsp;
may be unearthing the discovery of a lifetime.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:34.800
The Dig is one of those movies that will have&nbsp;
history hounds scrambling once it's finished to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:38.480
learn more about the true story surrounding&nbsp;
it. But despite concerning itself with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:43.680
monumental and historic find, this is mostly a&nbsp;
character-driven tale. Mulligan and Fiennes both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:47.600
give it their all, and many critics have lauded&nbsp;
the film's subdued pacing and moving drama.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:55.920
"Life is very fleeting. I've learnt&nbsp;
that. It has moments you should seize."

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:00.400
It would be incredibly easy to just&nbsp;
scroll right past Space Sweepers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:05.200
but if you're a fan of sci-fi action, that would&nbsp;
be a huge mistake. This adventure film has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:09.760
referred to by several outlets as Korea's first&nbsp;
"space blockbuster," and it features some great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:14.400
character work, a fun and compelling story,&nbsp;
and some surprisingly strong visual effects.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:18.800
Space Sweepers takes place in a future where&nbsp;
Earth is on the verge of being uninhabitable.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:22.080
Select wealthy individuals are given&nbsp;
a chance to live on a space station,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:26.240
but most of the human population is stuck&nbsp;
breathing the poisoned air of our atmosphere.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:30.560
In this world, the eponymous "space sweepers''&nbsp;
are essentially sky pirates, cruising through the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:35.440
atmosphere to collect debris and sell it for cash.&nbsp;
The movie's main cast is doing just that when they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:40.320
discover something extremely valuable — both for&nbsp;
the ruling classes and the future of the planet.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:44.640
Space Sweepers is a pretty wild ride, and has&nbsp;
even been cited by some critics as a decent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:48.320
substitute for a Star Wars or Marvel&nbsp;
movie. Who knows? Maybe they're right.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:52.560
Sometimes, all you want is a little&nbsp;
rom-com convenience to pick you up.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:55.760
To All the Boys: Always and Forever&nbsp;
is the third film in the franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.760 --> 00:04:00.000
and it'll give you exactly that — namely,&nbsp;
high school drama, blown up to the nth degree,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.760
with everything working out and wrapping up&nbsp;
nicely in the end. Based on the book trilogy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:08.000
by Jenny Han, Always and Forever is a fitting&nbsp;
and fun conclusion to the All the Boys saga.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:12.720
The trilogy follows Lara Jean, a high schooler who&nbsp;
writes letters to boys she has a crush on and then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:17.360
locks the notes in her closet. One day, those&nbsp;
letters get sent out as a prank, and Lara Jean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:21.680
has to navigate some very awkward situations&nbsp;
when the recipients come asking about them.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:25.760
More specifically, Always and Forever finds&nbsp;
Lara and her boyfriend preparing for college&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:29.760
and the possibility of having to navigate a&nbsp;
long-distance relationship. Sure, it's silly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:33.840
but it's remarkably well-acted and pretty&nbsp;
darn charming for a high school rom-com.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.920
If you're not really a fan of romantic comedies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:39.120
let your guard down a bit and give it a&nbsp;
whirl — it's way better than you think.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.240
What's that? Idris Elba riding a horse?

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:43.300
“Sold!"

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:46.800
And hey, turns out there's a whole&nbsp;
movie centered on the premise:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:50.720
Concrete Cowboy. On top of being a really&nbsp;
impressive piece of character drama,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:54.720
it's also based on a real-life group. The&nbsp;
Fletcher Street Urban Riding Club is made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:58.080
up of inner-city cowboys who still&nbsp;
operate in downtown Philadelphia.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:01.600
Concrete Cowboy is about a young man&nbsp;
named Cole who moves to Philadelphia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:05.840
to hopefully set his life straight through his&nbsp;
estranged father, played by Elba. Cole becomes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:09.760
enamored with the urban cowboy lifestyle,&nbsp;
but trouble tends to follow him around.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:14.000
It all comes to a head when some of Cole's&nbsp;
friends cross paths with a local drug dealer.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:17.200
Caleb McLaughlin and Elba give great&nbsp;
performances here, and their supporting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:21.680
cast also put on a good show. The big draw of&nbsp;
Concrete Cowboy, however, is the fascinating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:25.800
culture of the riders — and, naturally,&nbsp;
lots of lovely shots of beautiful horses.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:31.600
Apparently, a fear of people stuck in small spaces&nbsp;
struggling to survive gained some traction during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:35.680
the pandemic. Who would've guessed it? And if&nbsp;
you're a fan of foreign films, then you'll find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:40.400
Oxygen to be a breathtaking thriller — one that'll&nbsp;
keep you guessing right up until the end credits.

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:45.040
This French-language film stars Mélanie Laurent&nbsp;
as a woman who wakes up inside a cryogenic sleep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:49.760
chamber, because her oxygen is running dangerously&nbsp;
low. She has no memory of what she's doing there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:54.400
and is forced to fix things before the air runs&nbsp;
out. It doesn't help that her AI assistant isn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:58.480
giving her the answers she needs, either.&nbsp;
Worse still, her near-total isolation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:02.960
and oxygen deprivation leads her to question&nbsp;
everything she's experiencing in the first place.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:06.720
Oxygen is directed by horror regular&nbsp;
Alexandre Aja, who recently helmed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:10.400
the surprisingly entertaining Crawl, so&nbsp;
it's got some bona fides attached to it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:13.760
It's also carried almost entirely&nbsp;
by Laurent's impressive performance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:17.840
and despite that hugely stressful premise, the&nbsp;
central mystery is actually a whole lot of fun.

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:23.280
When a movie boasts a cast like Stowaway, it's&nbsp;
hard not to take notice. Stowaway is a thriller&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:27.520
that follows a small team of scientists headed&nbsp;
to Mars. Toni Collette plays the captain of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:32.000
mission, Anna Kendrick the medical officer, and&nbsp;
Daniel Dae Kim a biologist researching ways to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:36.000
bring plant life to the red planet. Of course, the&nbsp;
title of the movie should tip you off that there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:40.720
someone else involved — someone who isn't supposed&nbsp;
to be there. What follows is a claustrophobic and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:45.280
intense look at how far these people will go to&nbsp;
keep everyone safe on an already dangerous trip.

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:48.080
One of the most interesting choices&nbsp;
Stowaway makes is not letting the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:51.920
audience hear any of the communications&nbsp;
the team has outside of one another.

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:54.560
"I still need this crew to perform critical tasks.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:58.560
No, they cannot do that if&nbsp;
they are devastated by guilt!"

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:04.560
It all feels incredibly intimate, as any chatter&nbsp;
with mission control is entirely one-sided.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:07.040
You want to know what they're saying&nbsp;
down there, but you're stuck on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:11.120
ship with the characters instead. It really&nbsp;
doesn't get much more intense than this.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:15.520
If you only stick to the English-language&nbsp;
section of Netflix, you're gonna miss out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:18.960
on some really great titles. A&nbsp;
perfect example is Skater Girl,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:23.280
a film about a young girl from a rural community&nbsp;
in India falling in love with skateboarding.

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:26.800
Skater Girl is a classic fish-out-of-water&nbsp;
sports movie. You know the drill:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:30.320
A teenager is introduced to some new&nbsp;
activity with wide-eyed amazement,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:34.480
overcomes difficulties and prejudices to learn&nbsp;
it, and eventually begins inspiring others with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:38.640
their passion. But a few other aspects of&nbsp;
Skater Girl help it stand out from the pack.

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:42.720
The first is the impressive casting. There&nbsp;
aren't a lot of recognizable actors here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:47.360
unless you regularly watch Hindi-language films,&nbsp;
but everyone puts on a great performance — most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:51.760
notably the lead, Rachel Sanchita Gupta,&nbsp;
in her first-ever professional role.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:55.920
And then there's the cinematography. Everything&nbsp;
about Skater Girl is beautiful to look at,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:59.600
and the skateboarding scenes are nothing less&nbsp;
than stunning. The whole movie feels full&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:03.680
of life and kinetic energy, making it that&nbsp;
much easier to lose yourself in its story.

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:09.120
It seems unlikely you missed Army of the Dead,&nbsp;
as Netflix put a whole lot of hype behind its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:14.160
release. Even still, this is one of their most&nbsp;
ambitious original titles in quite some time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:18.160
and it ticks a lot of boxes for a lot of&nbsp;
people. After all, it's a zombie-heist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:22.160
movie with an impressive ensemble cast,&nbsp;
written and directed by Zack Snyder.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:25.920
And if that caught your attention, then&nbsp;
this one is probably right up your alley.

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:30.080
Dave Bautista stars as a former special ops&nbsp;
soldier who's tasked with taking a team into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:35.360
Las Vegas to steal millions of dollars from a&nbsp;
casino vault. Oh, and Vegas has been barricaded to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:40.640
contain a zombie outbreak inside the city. Oh, and&nbsp;
a nuke is going to be dropped on it in a few days.

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:44.560
Army of the Dead is a fun mashup of&nbsp;
"one last job" heist and zombie horror,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:48.160
and a truly motley crew of international&nbsp;
stars join Bautista on his mission.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:53.840
"I'm not trying to be the bad guy, but we&nbsp;
should be incentivized to let him die."

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:57.600
All in all, this makes for a&nbsp;
lot of fun, a ton of slow-mo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:01.440
and even more crazy violence. This&nbsp;
is Zack Snyder at his Snyderiest.

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:05.920
Some of the best horror movies explore the&nbsp;
lengths to which people will go in order to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:10.080
protect the people they love, and Blood&nbsp;
Red Sky is an excellent example of this.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:13.920
This brutal and gory creature feature has a&nbsp;
surprising amount of heart packed in there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:18.640
considering all that violence. And it's far more&nbsp;
fun than the plot might lead you to believe.

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:22.320
Here are the basics: A woman named Nadja&nbsp;
and her son are on an overnight flight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:26.080
and she's clearly suffering and trying to hide&nbsp;
it from him. But when a group of terrorists&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:29.840
hijack the plane and kill the flight crew,&nbsp;
they get much more than they bargained for.&nbsp;

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:32.960
Nadja is unable to keep her inner&nbsp;
beast at bay, and she transforms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:36.880
into a savage vampire that begins picking&nbsp;
off the many threats to her son's life.

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:41.280
More than anything, the movie's creature design&nbsp;
and inventive kills are a blast to watch.&nbsp;

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:44.880
Fans of more brutal, feral vampire&nbsp;
flicks are sure to enjoy this one — and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:47.760
horror lovers in general will almost&nbsp;
certainly get a kick out of it, too.

